Z||000002||fropuff||12-02-2000||07:20 PM||||You can find some information on the other page.  I got mine painted in mid-August.  Cost me around $400 for supplies and $0 for labor!  He wanted a dinner gift certificate, but the restaurant screwed up and didn't bill us yet.  I did wet sand (sucks), mask, remove the lights and moldings. You probably won't find labor this cheap unless you do it yourself.  You might find someone to do it for around $500, a grand total of about $1000.  Or you could bring it to MAACO for $300.  I'm bringing it there to get the ground effects done next summer.  Might want to do your own masking and all that crap, but the warranty might be void.  I got a quote for the roof panels (JUST the roof panels-with a sunroof) for $800 from a popular shop.  They do a very nice job, but that was a little high for me.  So I brought it to the cheap labor guy.  I think he did a very nice job for $400, especially now that I've waxed it.  I have to buff it out again; had a little slide into the woods, but then it'll look like a 9 out of 10.  Sometimes the garage-type shops are just as good as the professionals.  Preparation is the key, however.  Good luck.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
